#X obj 60 40 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty pdoly8.i~\ and\ pdoly8~ 24 6 0 22 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 76 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty 4-voice\ Poly-800\ tone\ generation\ -\ MSM5232\ foot\ synthesis 24 6 0 16 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 120 pdoly8.i~ 1;
#X text 190 120 <- click it: the editor, f 64;
#X obj 60 160 dac~;
#X obj 60 206 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty pdoly8.i~ 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 234 pdoly8.i~ is the whole instrument in one object: pdoly8~ \, the editor \, the controller layer \, the Launchkey pads with their translator p8nav and the display \, MIDI in and out. Put it in a patch \, connect the two left outlets to dac~ and play. Click it to open the editor \, see Editor. \; Argument 1 is the MIDI channel (0 or none = 1 \, the setting ch1) \, argument 2 the channel of the pads (0 or none = 10 \, the Drums Channel). Notes and pitch bend come from notein and bendin inside \, the controller layer follows ch1. Several pdoly8.i~ do not get in each other's way \, each has its own editor. \; pdoly8~ is the bare engine inside \, for patches of your own: notes as lists from notein \, inlet 2 a signal for FM (extfm) \, outlet 3 its events. Open pdoly8.i~ to see the wiring., f 64;
#X obj 60 472 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Editor 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 500 The editor is the window of pdoly8.i~. Every change shows up in it (controller \, presets \, messages \, random). \; Rows of 8: rows 1 to 11 are the pages of the controller layer (page k on the Launchkey = row k) \, then the rows without CC \, titled as in Controls. Each cell: name and CC number \, label \, a slider and a number box with the value as from a pot (0 to 127) \, the box beside it the real value. \; PRESETS DELAY RANDOM band: factory N (factory program 0 to 63 \, = program 11 to 88 of the Poly-800 II) \, MIDI ch (ch1 \, 0 = omni: notes and the controller layer follow it \, presets and defaults keep it) \, the user bank (user N loads a slot \, store to N only chooses one \, save patch stores the sound there and writes the file \, load bank reads it again \, factory init fills the user bank with the 64 factory programs: the file only changes with save patch) \, the delay presets of the Poly-800 II and random sounds: pluck \, bass \, lead \, brass \, pad \, strings \, total (keep a good one with store to and save patch). \; POLY-800 II SYSEX band (the user bank): send bank sends it as a data dump to MIDI out (the Poly-800's MIDI channel must match) \, write .syx saves it as a file. A dump from the synth (start it there) and read .syx replace the user bank \, save patch keeps it. The memory outside the programs (sequencer \, chord memory) comes from the factory dump \, loaded at start. The Launchkey does not pass MIDI from the computer to its MIDI out: use a MIDI interface., f 64;
#X obj 60 914 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Launchkey 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 942 Launchkey: the Novation Launchkey Mini MK4 with the custom firmware maltepeter2000/launchkey_firmware \, set up the same for every instrument of bela-workstation (launchkey/README.md there). \; p8cc 1: the controller layer. Encoders in mode Custom 1 send CC pages from 20 in rows of 8 on the keys channel \, every change made elsewhere goes back to them on the send channel (txchannel of pdoly8~) \, CC 3 asks for all values. \; p8pads 10: the pads in Drum mode (notes 36-51 on channel 10 \, the Drums Channel): top row 36 factory + \, 37 user + \, 38 init (press twice within a second) \, 39-43 own \, bottom row 44 factory - \, 45 user - \, 46 save \, 47-51 own. Own pads of pdoly8~: 39-43 random pluck \, bass \, lead \, brass \, pad \, 47 random strings \, 48 random total. \; Storing asks first: save once shows Store to? and the user slot played or stored last (savearm) \, user + / - choose the slot (saveslot 1 / -1 \, nothing is recalled) \, save again stores there and writes the user bank (save). Any other pad or 10 s cancel (savecancel). Own pads and init after its first press show what they do on the display. \; Pad colours \, sent by p8pads itself with noteout on channel 10 (velocity = colour + 32 x mode): factory blue \, user and save green (the user bank) \, init orange (flashing while the second press is awaited) \, save flashing while it asks and white for a moment when stored \, own pads purple \, free pads dark. They go out at load \, on leds \, and when the Launchkey asks for them (CC 3 = 127 on channel 10 \, sent when Drum mode is selected). \; p8nav: turns the pad messages into what pdoly8~ understands (its user bank is kept in Pd) \, sends the display lines of patch changes and stores and passes those of pdoly8~ on. \; lkdisplay: the display lines (display <title> <value>: the control you turn \, Preset \, User \, Init or Stored with the patch name) as SysEx for the Launchkey's display -> midiout., f 64;
#X obj 60 1484 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlet 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1512 1 <pitch> <velocity> and the messages below., f 64;
#X obj 60 1542 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1570 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: value \, dump \, norm \, disp \, info \, channel \, \;   display lines., f 64;
#X obj 60 1648 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ user\ bank 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1676 The user bank (64 sounds \, text \, p8user-bank.txt) is kept by the editor and the pad translator. In pdoly8.i~ it is the file in the folder of your patch \, so every project keeps its own. Until it is there the file beside pdoly8~ is read \, or else the 64 factory programs. save patch in the editor and the pads' save write the file beside your patch. Save the patch first \, an unsaved patch has no folder of its own. \; The factory programs come from presets/poly800mk2-factory.txt beside pdoly8~. tools/p8sysex.py converts Poly-800 II SysEx dumps to preset text and back. For lists of your own: p8factory and p8user name (a [text define -k name] saved with your patch) send 'dump pdoly8 ...' messages \, store N writes., f 64;
#X obj 60 1882 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1910 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <setting> <value>: e.g. cut 60 (all names: Controls) \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; delay flanger / chorus1 / chorus2 / slap / long / off \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices \, times bnd semitones \; n <name> <0-127>: a setting from a pot \, CV or MIDI CC \, \;   scaled to its range (switches in zones \, 64 = 0 if bipolar) \; nget <name> <tag>: outlet 3 gets norm <tag> <0-127> \, \;   the setting as a pot position (for pickup) \; ninfo <name>: outlet 3 gets info <name> <0-127> <value> \, \;   pot position and value with unit. Every change is also \;   reported this way by itself (editor \, controller layer) \; disp <name>: outlet 3 gets disp <label> <value> \, \;   two symbols for a display (OLED) \; oled <host> <port>: changed settings to O2O (an OLED) as \;   OSC \, sent from a thread of its own \; oledtext <line 1> <line 2>: two lines for the OLED \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 3 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 3 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly \; random <kind> [seed]: a new sound \, kind = pluck \, bass \, lead \, \;   brass \, pad \, strings or total (the MIDI channel stays) \; syxin <byte>: bytes from [sysexin] \, a whole data dump gives \;   bank <n> pdoly8 ... for the 64 programs on outlet 3 \; syxread <file> \, syxwrite <file>: a .syx file \; syxbank <n> pdoly8 ...: a preset into program n (0-63) \; syxsend: the dump as syxbyte <b> on outlet 3 (-> [midiout]) \;   needs a dump received or read first (sequencer \, chord \;   memory and MIDI channel are kept from it), f 64;
#X obj 60 2468 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Timbre\ (har1\ /\ har2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2496 The 15 distinct timbres of the original \, dark to bright: \; 0: 16' / saw net 9: 16'2' / 18: 16'4'2' / 27: 16'4' / \; 36: 16'8'4' / 45: all / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: 16'8' / \; square net 73: 16'8' / 82: 16'8'4' / 91: 16'4' / \; 100: 16'4'2' / 109: all / 118: 16'8'2' / 127: 16'2'. \; One foot or the net per step. The combinations without 16' \; are the same waves higher: use oct1 / oct2 2-4. \; A fading foot rises in power \, so the morph has no dips., f 64;
#X obj 60 2638 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2666 DCO settings: Timbre \, octave and the modulations of the tone generators. Beyond har and oct nothing here is on the Poly-800. All edges stay band-limited. In this order: timbre \, octave \, PWM \, Walsh loop \, sync \, ring. \; Cross mod: Linear FM of the counter rate \, through zero (the counter runs backwards) above index 1 \, every edge band-limited. Not on the Poly-800. \; Filter & DEG3 settings: One 4-pole VCF for the instrument (NJM2069) and one DEG3 for all voices \, measured on a Poly-800 II. \; MG settings: One triangle MG for the instrument \, measured on a Poly-800 II. It also drives hmg \, pwm1/2 \, wsm and swm (DCO settings). \; Delay settings: The digital delay of the Poly-800 II (71-75) \, measured: the echo is in phase on the left output and inverted on the right (a mono sum cancels it). A gate ends the echo train \, changing a value mutes the echo for a moment \, as on the original. \; DEG1 & DEG2 settings: Each voice's DCO1 and DCO2 have their own 6-stage DEG as on the Poly-800. Measured on a Poly-800 II: level 0-31 is about (L/31)^2 \, attack rises linearly (31: about 9 s) \, decay \, slope and release fall at a constant dB per second (31: about 18 s to -40 dB). env1 / env2 (Controls) morph through: 0 gate / 1 short pluck / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. \; Performance: Laid over the sound \, not stored in it (Launchkey page 9 MORE). A sound recalled sets atk and rel back to 0. \; Portamento: Not on the Poly-800., f 64;
#X obj 60 3128 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3156 In the order of the editor: one heading per row \, the same title as the row there \, page k on the controller is row k. Each line: name (the label in the editor) \, range \, CC number and what it does., f 64;
#X obj 60 3234 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 1\ \ PLAY\ \ CC\ 20\ 21\ 22\ 23\ 24\ 25\ 26\ 27 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3262 har1 (Timbre 1) 0..127 \, CC 20: Timbre of DCO1 \, one knob \;   through all 15 distinct original timbres \, dark to bright: 0 \;   16' / 9-64 saw net (16'2' \, 16'4'2' \, 16'4' \, 16'8'4' \, all at \;   45 \, 16'8'2' \, 16'8') / 73-127 square net (16'8' \, 16'8'4' \, \;   16'4' \, 16'4'2' \, all \, 16'8'2' \, 16'2'). One foot or the net \;   per step \, no jumps. Combinations without 16' = oct1 2-4. \;   Default 45. \; oct1 (Octave 1) -1..4 \, CC 21: -1 0 1 = LOW MID HIGH \, 2-4: the \;   feet one to three octaves higher (the combinations without \;   16'). Default 0. \; har2 (Timbre 2) 0..127 \, CC 22: Timbre of DCO2 \, same path. \;   Default 45. \; oct2 (Octave 2) -1..4 \, CC 23: -1 0 1 = LOW MID HIGH \, 2-4: the \;   feet one to three octaves higher (the combinations without \;   16'). Default 0. \; env1 (Env1 morph) 0..127 \, CC 24: Envelope of DCO1 (DEG1) \, one \;   knob: 0 gate / 1 very short pluck (no fade from the gate) / \;   24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / \;   127 long pad. -1 = own values a1 ... r1. Default 0. \; env2 (Env2 morph) 0..127 \, CC 25: Envelope of DCO2 (DEG2) \, the \;   same \, -1 = own values a2 ... r2. Default 0. \; lev1 (Level 1) 0..127 \, CC 26: Level of DCO1. Default 127. \; lev2 (Level 2) 0..127 \, CC 27: Level of DCO2 (every voice has \;   both DCOs). Above full scale (lev1 + lev2 > 127) both are \;   scaled down together. Default 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 3676 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 2\ \ FILTER\ \ CC\ 28\ 29\ 30\ 31\ 33\ 34\ 35\ 36 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3704 cut (Cutoff) 0..99 \, CC 28: 0-99 = 66 Hz - 20 kHz \, 13 steps per \;   octave. Default 99. \; res (Resonance) 0..15 \, CC 29: 0-15 \, an uncompensated ladder \;   (the bass falls as it rises) \, no self-oscillation. Default \;   0. \; egi (EG depth) 0..15 \, CC 30: EG INT 0-15 \, DEG3 moves the \;   cutoff up to 7.9 octaves. Default 0. \; kbd (Key track) 0..2 \, CC 31: key tracking of the highest key: \;   0 off \, 2 full (1:1 \, C4 nominal) \, 1 half (1:2 \, C6 nominal). \;   Default 0. \; env3 (Env3 morph) 0..127 \, CC 33: DEG3 morph as env1 (see \;   Controls) \, -1 = own values. Default 0. \; vcut (Vel>cutoff) 0..127 \, CC 34: velocity to the cutoff: at \;   127 a soft key is up to 5 octaves lower \, full velocity plays \;   the cut set (one VCF: the last key counts). Default 0. \; drv (Drive) 0..127 \, CC 35: overdrive (not on the Poly-800) \, \;   soft clipping \, 0-127 = 0-48 dB more gain with level makeup. \;   Default 0. \; drvp (Drive pos) 0..1 \, CC 36: 0 post: after the VCF \, denser \;   with res and chords \, 1 pre: into the VCF \, which rounds the \;   distortion off (warmer). Default 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 4054 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 3\ \ OSC\ \ CC\ 37\ 39\ 40\ 41\ 42\ 43\ 44\ 45 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4082 intv (Interval) 0..12 \, CC 37: Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 in \;   semitones \, 0-12 \, as stored on the Poly-800 II. Default 0. \; detn (Detune) 0..127 \, CC 39: Detune of DCO2 downwards: the \;   original's 4 steps 0 \, 6.5 \, 13 \, 26 cents lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, \;   127. Default 0. \; pw1 (PW 1) 0..127 \, CC 40: pulse width 0-127 = 3-97 % \, 64 = \;   square. Every foot becomes the AND of itself and a copy \;   shifted by part of its period (pulse staircases on the saw \;   net). Default 64. \; pw2 (PW 2) 0..127 \, CC 41: pulse width 0-127 = 3-97 % \, 64 = \;   square. Every foot becomes the AND of itself and a copy \;   shifted by part of its period (pulse staircases on the saw \;   net). Default 64. \; pwm1 (PWM 1) -127..127 \, CC 42: the MG moves the width \, \;   -127..127 = +-47 %. Negative turns the direction round: pwm1 \;   60 with pwm2 -60 makes the two DCOs widen and narrow against \;   each other. Default 0. \; pwm2 (PWM 2) -127..127 \, CC 43: the MG moves the width \, \;   -127..127 = +-47 %. Negative turns the direction round: pwm1 \;   60 with pwm2 -60 makes the two DCOs widen and narrow against \;   each other. Default 0. \; drft (Drift) 0..127 \, CC 44: analogue drift (not on the \;   Poly-800 \, whose pitch comes from a crystal and dividers) \, \;   like the slop / vintage knob of newer Sequential \;   instruments: every DCO of every voice wanders slowly and on \;   its own (at 127 about +-3 cents \, peaks about 8) \, each note's \;   envelopes run a little faster or slower (+-20 % \, DEG3 too) \, \;   the MG rate wanders +-10 % and the cutoff +-0.2 octaves. 0 = \;   exact. Default 0. \; nois (Noise) 0..15 \, CC 45: white noise 0-15 \, its VCA follows \;   DEG3. Default 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 4592 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 4\ \ WALSH-RING\ \ CC\ 46\ 47\ 48\ 49\ 50\ 51\ 52\ 53 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4620 wsh1 (Walsh pos 1) 0..127 \, CC 46: position on the loop 0-127 \;   (0: 16' / 17: 16'x4' / 59: 2' / 85: all four / 119: 16'x8' / \;   127 = 0 again). Default 0. \; wsh2 (Walsh pos 2) 0..127 \, CC 47: position on the loop 0-127 \;   (0: 16' / 17: 16'x4' / 59: 2' / 85: all four / 119: 16'x8' / \;   127 = 0 again). Default 0. \; wmx1 (Walsh mix 1) 0..127 \, CC 48: mix from the normal feet (0) \;   to the loop (127). Default 0. \; wmx2 (Walsh mix 2) 0..127 \, CC 49: mix from the normal feet (0) \;   to the loop (127). Default 0. \; wse (EG3>Walsh) -127..127 \, CC 50: DEG3 moves the position by \;   up to wse steps (-127..127) \, e.g. a bright attack falling \;   into the 16'. wsm and wse act where wmx is above 0. Default \;   0. \; wsm (MG>Walsh) 0..127 \, CC 51: the MG moves the position +-wsm \;   steps (127: the whole loop \, a sweeping \, vocal sound - try \;   mgr 2-8). Default 0. \; ring (Ring mod) 0..127 \, CC 52: 0-127 \, DCO2 is multiplied by a \;   +-1 wave of DCO1 (XOR \, the ring modulation of square waves). \;   At 127 only sum and difference tones remain \, lev1 0 for the \;   pure ring sound. Default 0. \; rmf (Ring source) 0..14 \, CC 53: the modulator \, a step 0-14 on \;   the Walsh loop of DCO1: 0 its 16' (softest) \, 1 8' \, 3 4' \, 7 \;   2' \, 10 all four feet \, back down to 14 16'x8'. Steps towards \;   7 move the sidebands further apart: stronger \, more metallic. \;   Default 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 5050 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 5\ \ SYNC-XMOD\ \ CC\ 54\ 55\ 56\ 57\ 58\ 59\ 60\ 61 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5078 sync (Sync) 0..1 \, CC 54: 1: DCO2's counter restarts at every \;   16' period of DCO1 \, at the exact sub-sample time. Default 0. \; swp2 (DCO2 pitch) 0..36 \, CC 55: DCO2 offset 0-36 semitones \, \;   continuous (0.28 per CC step). Whole intervals: intv. \;   Default 0. \; swe (EG3>DCO2) 0..72 \, CC 56: DEG3 adds up to 0-72 semitones to \;   DCO2. Default 0. \; swm (MG>DCO2) 0..24 \, CC 57: the MG adds +-0-24 semitones to \;   DCO2. Screaming sync: sync 1 \, lev1 low \, lev2 high \, swe \;   40-72 \, a falling DEG3 (d3 \, su3 0) \, res and drv up. The \;   sweeps also work without sync. Default 0. \; xmod (Cross mod) 0..127 \, CC 58: cross mod as on the Jupiter-8 \;   (X-MOD): DCO2 of the same voice modulates the pitch of DCO1 \, \;   0-127 = index 0-16 (1 at about 32). The modulator is DCO2's \;   wave without its level or envelope \, so lev2 0 gives pure \;   cross mod. intv and detn set the ratio (intv 7: a fifth \, \;   detn: slow beating) \, with sync 1 and a DCO2 sweep (swe \, swm) \;   the classic sync-and-cross-mod lead. Needs DCO2: mode DOUBLE \;   (every voice has both DCOs here). Default 0. \; extfm (Ext FM) 0..127 \, CC 59: the signal at the right inlet \;   (about -1..1: osc~ \, adc~ \, a CV) modulates both DCOs \, 0-127 = \;   index 0-16. Default 0. \; xme (EG3>Xmod) -127..127 \, CC 60: DEG3 moves the cross mod \;   index by up to +-16 (-127..127 \, quadratic): a falling DEG3 \;   with xme 80 gives a bright \, clangy attack that settles. \;   Default 0. \; xmm (MG>Xmod) 0..127 \, CC 61: the MG moves the cross mod index \;   by +-0..16 (rate mgr \, delay mgd). Default 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 5540 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 6\ \ MG\ \ CC\ 62\ 63\ 70\ 71\ 72\ 73\ 74 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5568 mgr (MG rate) 0..15 \, CC 62: frequency in steps 0-15 as \;   parameter 81 (0: 0.29 Hz / 3: 1.26 / 8: 5.2 / 15: 19 Hz). \;   Any frequency in Hz as a message: mgf 4.5 (mgr then shows \;   -1). Default 8. \; mgd (MG delay) 0..15 \, CC 63: delay 0-15 (82: 0.47 s at 5 \, 1.55 \;   s at 15) from the first key \, then full depth. Default 0. \; mgi (Vibrato) 0..200 \, CC 70: depth on the pitch in cents (83: \;   12.4 cents per step \, 186 at 15) \, a 14.5 Hz low-pass makes \;   fast vibrato shallower \, as on the original. Default 0. \; mgv (MG>cutoff) 0..15 \, CC 71: MG to the VCF 0-15 (84: +-7.9 \;   octaves at 15). Default 0. \; hmg (MG>timbre) 0..127 \, CC 72: the MG moves har1 and har2 by \;   +-hmg steps \, 127 = through the whole timbre path (rate mgr \, \;   delay mgd). Default 0. \; mgw (MG wave) 0..3 \, CC 73: MG wave: 0 triangle (the Poly-800) \, \;   1 sine \, 2 square \, 3 noise (a new random value each cycle \, \;   sample and hold). Square and noise get 2 ms edges \, so \;   nothing clicks. Not on the Poly-800. Default 0. \; mgk (MG retrig) 0..1 \, CC 74: 1: every key restarts the MG \;   cycle (noise draws a new value) \, so every note starts its \;   vibrato or sweep the same way. 0: it runs freely \, as on the \;   original. Default 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 5934 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 7\ \ DELAY-EQ\ \ CC\ 76\ 77\ 78\ 79\ 80\ 81\ 82\ 83 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5962 dtim (Delay time) 0..99 \, CC 76: 0-99 = 4.2 ms - 1.08 s (70: \;   216 ms). Default 30. \; dfb (Delay fback) 0..15 \, CC 77: feedback 0-15 (15: -3.1 dB per \;   echo). Default 0. \; dmf (Del mod rate) 0..31 \, CC 78: mod rate 0-31 = 0.05-5 Hz. \;   Default 0. \; dmi (Del mod dpth) 0..31 \, CC 79: mod depth 0-31 (31: the time \;   swings 1:5 \, about 10 dB less per 10 steps below). Default 0. \; dlev (Delay level) 0..15 \, CC 80: echo level 0-15 \, 0 = off. \;   Default 0. \; dgld (Delay change) 0..1 \, CC 81: 1: changes glide (time like a \;   tape \, feedback and level smoothed) \, for MIDI CC and \;   modulation \, 0: every change mutes the echo for 40 ms \, as on \;   the original. Default 1. \; treb (Treble) -6..6 \, CC 82: EQ -6..6 (76/77 \, measured: about 4 \;   dB at 3 \, 10 dB at 6 \, shelves at 4.3 kHz and 115 Hz). Default \;   0. \; bass (Bass) -6..6 \, CC 83: EQ -6..6 (76/77 \, measured: about 4 \;   dB at 3 \, 10 dB at 6 \, shelves at 4.3 kHz and 115 Hz). Default \;   0., f 64;
#X obj 60 6296 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 8\ \ PLAY\ MODE\ \ CC\ 85\ 86\ 87\ 89\ 90\ 91\ 92\ 93 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6324 port (Portamento) 0..127 \, CC 85: glide time 0-127 = off to 3 \;   s. Default 0. \; pmod (Glide mode) 0..2 \, CC 86: where a glide starts: 0 from \;   the last note played \, 1 from the note this voice played \;   before \, 2 from the last note only while another key is still \;   held (legato glide). pmod is not a mono / poly switch. \;   Default 0. \; mono (Voice mode) 0..1 \, CC 87: 0 poly (4 voices) \, 1 mono: one \;   voice \, the last key wins. Default 0. \; retr (Mono retrig) 0..1 \, CC 89: in mono \, 1: every key restarts \;   the envelopes \, 0: legato \, only the first key of a phrase \;   restarts them \, further keys (and going back to a held one) \;   only change the pitch. Default 1. \; vamp (Vel>level) 0..127 \, CC 90: velocity to the level of each \;   voice (both DCOs \, not on the Poly-800): 0 off \, 127 level = \;   velocity. Default 0. \; bnd (Bend range) 0..12 \, CC 91: bend range in semitones \;   (original: up to 7). Pitch bend from a MIDI keyboard comes \;   in through [bendin] at the top. Default 2. \; sprd (Stereo sprd) 0..127 \, CC 92: stereo spread of the 4 \;   voices 0-127. Default 0. \; mrph (Smoothing) 0..100 \, CC 93: smoothing time in ms of every \;   continuous setting (timbre \, levels \, cutoff \, resonance \, FM \, \;   ring \, drive \, noise \, DCO2 pitch \, detune \, vibrato \, EG depth \;   ...) \, so MIDI CC steps become ramps. 0 = none. Default 25., f 64;
#X obj 60 6738 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 9\ \ MORE\ \ CC\ 94\ 95\ 102\ 103\ 104\ 105\ 106 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6766 atk (Attack all) -63..63 \, CC 94: attack of DEG1 and DEG2 \, \;   release of DEG1 \, DEG2 and DEG3 \, -63..63 = -31..+31 DEG steps \;   on top of the sound's own or morphed values. Default 0. \; rel (Release all) -63..63 \, CC 95: attack of DEG1 and DEG2 \, \;   release of DEG1 \, DEG2 and DEG3 \, -63..63 = -31..+31 DEG steps \;   on top of the sound's own or morphed values. Default 0. \; vol (Volume) 0..127 \, CC 102: output volume \, 100 = 0 dB \, 127 = \;   +4 dB \, square law. Set up once \, defaults and presets keep \;   it. Default 100. \; tone (Output stage) 0..1 \, CC 103: 1: output stage measured on \;   a Poly-800 (54 Hz high-pass \, VCF \, 1 pole at 5 kHz) \, 0: raw \;   tone generators. Default 1. \; leak (Leak) 0..1 \, CC 104: 1: released voices stay at -55 dB \, \;   as on the original. Default 0. \; pol (EG polarity) 1..2 \, CC 105: 2 up \, 1 down. Default 2. \; trg (Env3 trig) 1..2 \, CC 106: 2 multi: every key restarts \;   DEG3 \, 1 single: only the first key of a phrase. Default 2., f 64;
#X obj 60 7052 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DEG1\ stages\ (sets\ env1\ to\ own)\ \ no\ CC 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 7080 a1 (Env1 attack) 0..31: env 1 attack \; d1 (Env1 decay) 0..31: env 1 decay \; bp1 (Env1 break) 0..31: env 1 break \; sl1 (Env1 slope) 0..31: env 1 slope \; su1 (Env1 sustain) 0..31: env 1 sustain \; r1 (Env1 release) 0..31: env 1 release, f 64;
#X obj 60 7190 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DEG2\ stages\ (sets\ env2\ to\ own)\ \ no\ CC 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
